-- =====================================================================
-- Session 155 — Matt 18 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 18's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2) -> S154 (Matt 17) extras-tier
-- coverage; Matt 18 lands as the King''s-fourth-major-discourse — the
-- kingdom-assembly''s-internal-architecture chapter. Five framework-
-- bearing narrative movements anchor the chapter:
--
--   (a) the greatness-as-child teaching (vv.1-5) — the disciples''
--       hierarchy-question (*who is the greatest in the kingdom of
--       heaven?*) surfacing after they had-disputed-on-the-road (Mark
--       9:33-34); the King''s-acted-parable of a little child set in
--       the midst in continuity with the Tanakh-prophetic-acted-parable
--       pattern (Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 20:2-4; Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 18:1-6;
--       Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 4-12, 24; Hoshea (Hosea) 1:2-9); the
--       *converted* (*straphēte*) substance as the Tanakh-*shuv*
--       (turning-back) of Devarim (Deuteronomy) 30:2, Yirmeyahu
--       (Jeremiah) 31:18-19, Hoshea (Hosea) 14:1, Yo''el (Joel) 2:12;
--       the four-fold child-substance — humility, receptiveness,
--       dependence, honesty — as the Tanakh-*anawim* pattern (Tehillim
--       (Psalm) 131:1-2, Tehillim (Psalm) 8:2, Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 11:6,
--       Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 57:15, Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 66:2, Mishlei
--       (Proverbs) 22:4); the kingdom-inversion restated at Matt
--       23:11-12 and apostolically at 1 Peter 5:5 (citing Mishlei
--       (Proverbs) 3:34) and Yaaqov (James) 4:10.
--   (b) the millstone-woe + sin-amputation + gehenna (vv.6-9) — the
--       *skandalisē* (cause-to-stumble) as the Tanakh-*mikshol*
--       (stumbling-block) of Vayikra (Leviticus) 19:14 and Yeshayahu
--       (Isaiah) 57:14; *little ones which believe in me* extending
--       beyond children-in-age to all believers-in-the-vulnerable-
--       position; the millstone-substance as deliberate-extreme-
--       hyperbole landing on the systems-and-leadership-who-perpetuate-
--       the-stumbling-block — institutional Christianity''s antinomian
--       doctrine, Hebrew-Roots false-inclusion gospel, the Pharisaic-
--       traditions-of-the-elders, the Galatian-circumcision-party; the
--       sin-amputation as the disciple''s-radical-disposition against
--       the disciple''s-own-stumbling-substance, parallel to Matt
--       5:29-30; the *gehenna of fire* as the Tanakh-*gei-Hinnom*
--       (Valley of the sons of Hinnom) judgment-substance (2 Kings
--       23:10; Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 7:32-33; Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 66:24)
--       — destruction, NOT the inherited-Christian-eternal-conscious-
--       torment doctrine read-back into the term.
--   (c) despise-not-the-little-ones + their-angels + the lost-sheep
--       parable (vv.10-14) — the *kataphronēsēte* (think-down-on)
--       inversion of the disciples'' v.1-hierarchy-disposition; the
--       little-ones'' messengers *do always behold the face of my
--       Father* per the Tanakh-and-Second-Temple guardian-messenger
--       pattern (Shemot (Exodus) 23:20, Tehillim (Psalm) 91:11, Daniel
--       10:13, Acts 12:15, Hebrews 1:14); *the Son of Adam is come to
--       save that which was lost* restating the King''s-mission-scope
--       of Matt 10:5-6 and Matt 15:24 — the lost-sheep-of-the-house-
--       of-Yashar''el (Israel) gathering per Red Line #7; the shepherd-
--       parable landing at two levels simultaneously: assembly''s-
--       internal-little-ones AND canon-wide lost-sheep-of-Yashar''el
--       (Israel) mission-scope; the shepherd-substance derived from
--       the Tanakh-Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34:11-13 (*behold, I, even
--       I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out*), Yirmeyahu
--       (Jeremiah) 50:6, Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 53:6; the Father''s-will-
--       substance apostolically restated at 2 Peter 3:9.
--   (d) FRAMEWORK-MAJOR — the assembly-discipline 4-step + binding-
--       and-loosing-extended + two-or-three-gathered (vv.15-20) —
--       step-one applying Vayikra (Leviticus) 19:17''s *thou shalt in
--       any wise rebuke thy neighbour;* step-two applying Devarim
--       (Deuteronomy) 19:15''s two-or-three-witnesses Tanakh-
--       evidentiary-standard (apostolically extended at 1 Timothy
--       5:19 to leadership-discipline); step-three''s *ekklēsia* as
--       the second-explicit-use after Matt 16:18 — the called-out-
--       ones of the gathering-of-the-scattered-seed in continuity
--       with the Tanakh-*qahal* (Shemot (Exodus) 19:5-6, Devarim
--       (Deuteronomy) 31:30, Tehillim (Psalm) 22:22); step-four''s
--       *as a heathen and a publican* as disposition-shift from
--       internal-assembly-member to mission-target, NOT permanent-
--       shunning; the binding-and-loosing extended from Kefa (Peter)-
--       alone at Matt 16:19 to the assembly-as-a-whole, with the
--       keys deriving from Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 22:22 and the locus-
--       classicus at Acts 15''s Yerushalayim (Jerusalem) Council;
--       *where two or three are gathered together in my name, there
--       am I in the midst of them* in continuity with Malachi 3:16''s
--       Tanakh-precedent — the corporate-gathering-in-the-King''s-
--       name, NOT the institutional-Christian-individualistic-prayer-
--       meeting reading.
--   (e) FRAMEWORK-MAJOR — the seventy-times-seven + Lamekh (Lamech)-
--       inversion + unforgiving-servant parable + grace-that-can-be-
--       lost (vv.21-35) — Kefa (Peter)''s *till seven times* doubling
--       the rabbinic-three-times-then-refuse standard; the King''s
--       *seventy times seven* as the deliberate inversion of Lamekh
--       (Lamech)''s *if Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamekh
--       (Lamech) seventy and sevenfold* at Bereshit (Genesis) 4:24 —
--       the Cainite-line''s-escalated-vengeance inverted into the
--       kingdom-line''s forgiveness-substance, in continuity with
--       Tehillim (Psalm) 103:8-12, Mikhah (Micah) 7:18-19, Yeshayahu
--       (Isaiah) 43:25; the unforgiving-servant parable''s 10,000-
--       talents naming impossibility-of-repayment (the disciple''s-
--       sin-debt before the Father); *splanchnistheis* (moved-in-
--       the-bowels) compassion granting more-than-the-petition; the
--       Tanakh-anchor at Vayikra (Leviticus) 25:10-14''s Jubilee
--       debt-release compressed into the single-transaction; the
--       parable''s most-direct-NT-articulation of the grace-that-can-
--       be-lost architecture — the forgiveness-given-is-reversed
--       when the disposition-the-forgiveness-was-given-to-form does
--       not form; the chapter-closing *from your hearts forgive not*
--       (v.35) as the heart-Torah of the new-covenant (Yirmeyahu
--       (Jeremiah) 31:33, Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27); the
--       institutional-Christian-once-saved-always-saved doctrine
--       ruled out — the cross opens the door home, the door remains
--       real (1 Corinthians 9:27''s *lest by any means... I myself
--       should be a castaway*).
--
-- The extras-library adds five framework-bearing thread-clusters for
-- Matt 18:
--   Thread 1 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): the Watcher-rebellion-as-the-
--     stumbling-block-architecture in 1 Enoch 8-22 — the wisdom-
--     stream''s articulation of the original-stumbling-block
--     architecture the King''s millstone-warning at vv.6-9 lands on.
--     1 Enoch 8:1-2''s Azâzêl teaching the substance of *skandalon*
--     to the children of men is the substance behind the King''s
--     *it must needs be that offences come.* The seed-war operating
--     architecturally from the watcher-fall through the present-age
--     is the architecture under the inevitability-of-offences the
--     King names at v.7; the woe to the man-by-whom-the-offence-
--     cometh is the same architecture 1 Enoch names the eternal
--     judgment-substance for at 1 Enoch 22:11.
--   Thread 2 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): the Lord-of-the-sheep-and-the-
--     gathering-in-the-Animal-Apocalypse — 1 Enoch 89-90 carries
--     the wisdom-stream''s most-direct shepherd-substance running
--     in parallel with Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34''s Tanakh-shepherd-
--     substance. The Lord-of-the-sheep walks the whole arc — the
--     scattering through the apostasy, the silence while the beasts
--     devour, the gathering at the consummation when *all feared the
--     Lord of the sheep.* The Matt 18 lost-sheep parable carries
--     the same shepherd-substance both at the assembly''s-internal-
--     level AND at the canon-wide lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-
--     Yashar''el (Israel) mission-scope per Red Line #7.
--   Thread 3: the reproof-and-restoration procedure in Sirach
--     (Ecclesiasticus) 19-21 — the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-
--     anchor for the four-step assembly-discipline pattern the King
--     teaches at vv.15-17. Sirach 19:13-17 walks the same procedure
--     the King will codify — admonish-the-friend first, weigh the
--     report against witnesses, give the brother place-of-the-
--     Most-High''s-law to repent. The substance Sirach names at the
--     wisdom-instruction-register the King institutionalizes at the
--     assembly''s-procedural-register.
--   Thread 4 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): the forgive-and-be-forgiven mercy-
--     met-with-mercy architecture in Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 27-28
--     and Testament of Gad — the wisdom-stream''s most-direct-
--     prefiguring of the King''s vv.21-35 forgiveness-architecture.
--     Sirach 28:1-7 carries the entire architecture in compressed
--     form: *forgive your neighbour the hurt that he has done to
--     you, so shall your sins also be forgiven* — the same
--     conditional-substance the King''s parable extends into full
--     narrative-form. Testament of Gad 62:3 names the *love one
--     another from the heart, and if a man sin against thee, speak
--     peaceably to him* the King''s v.15 procedure begins from.
--   Thread 5: the greatness-as-humility-and-the-proud-cast-down
--     in the wisdom-stream — Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 3 + Sirach 10
--     + 1 Enoch 46. The wisdom-stream had named the kingdom-
--     inversion-substance the King teaches at vv.1-5 — the great
--     are humbled, the lowly are exalted, the proud-princes are
--     cast-down from their thrones. The Son-of-Adam at 1 Enoch 46
--     is the One who-puts-down-kings-from-thrones — the
--     eschatological-architecture under the kingdom-inversion the
--     King names at the assembly-level.
--
-- Matt 18 does not surface framework-bearing Ascension of Isaiah
-- (vision-pivot, not assembly-internal-architecture), Jubilees,
-- Jasher, Adam-Eve Conflict, Apocalypse of Abraham, or Sonnini''s
-- Acts of Paul connections at S155. Historical-witness editions
-- (Josephus, M.R. James''s apocryphal NT, Lightfoot''s Apostolic
-- Fathers) remain deferred from V1 cross-refs per the historical-
-- witness one-way rule. The lookup view retains the S154 edition
-- set for forward compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `the-watcher-rebellion-as-the-stumbling-block-architecture-in-1-enoch`        (sort 312)
--   2. `the-lord-of-the-sheep-and-the-gathering-in-the-animal-apocalypse`            (sort 313)
--   3. `the-reproof-and-restoration-procedure-in-sirach`                             (sort 314)
--   4. `forgive-and-be-forgiven-the-mercy-met-with-mercy-architecture`               (sort 315)
--   5. `the-greatness-as-humility-and-the-proud-cast-down-in-the-wisdom-stream`      (sort 316)
--
-- 22 new cross_references rows at tier_required=''extras'' (Library
-- tier, $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=
-- ''complete_study'' (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the
-- chapter-end-card architecture established at S146 and prior: Layer 1
-- (per-verse cross-refs) visible to Library readers; Layer 2 (framework
-- thread callouts with summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion.
-- Every member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist. The seed-mechanism per framework-deep''s *Paternal Seed
-- and the Marriage-Covenant Absorption* section + Red Line #7
-- augmentation does not surface in Matt 18 (the chapter is internal to
-- the disciples and the assembly''s-internal-architecture — no foreign-
-- origin individuals or seed-distinction substance in the chapter).
-- Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el, Ya''aqov,
-- Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Mosheh''s, King''s, Father''s, Yahuah''s,
-- Yochanan''s, Kefa''s, Lamekh''s, Lord''s, etc.) and English
-- possessives (wisdom-stream''s, disciple''s, lord''s, servant''s,
-- assembly''s, kingdom''s, system''s, etc.) are escaped per SQL single-
-- quoted-string-literal convention (every internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 155 — Matt 18 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S154 view; retained for forward
-- compatibility even though Matt 18 surfaces only canon + enoch +
-- apocrypha + pseudepigrapha at S155.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s155_xref_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 22 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: the-watcher-rebellion-as-the-stumbling-block-architecture-in-1-enoch
  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 6, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 8, 1,
   '*And Azâzêl taught men to make swords, and knives, and shields, and breastplates ... and the metals of the earth and the art of working them ... and the use of antimony, and the beautifying of the eyelids, and all kinds of costly stones, and all colouring tinctures.* 1 Enoch 8:1 names THE architectural-root of the *skandalon* (stumbling-block) substance the King''s millstone-warning at Matt 18:6 lands-on. The framework reads the verse as the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the substance behind the seed-war: the watchers taught-the-children-of-men the substance that placed-the-stumbling-blocks across the way of the walker. The framework reads this in continuity with the Tanakh-*mikshol* of Vayikra (Leviticus) 19:14 (*thou shalt not curse the deaf, nor put a stumblingblock before the blind*) and Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 57:14 (*take up the stumblingblock out of the way of my people*); the architecture behind those Tanakh-commands is the architecture 1 Enoch names the source of. The little-ones-who-believe whom the King protects with the millstone-warning are the same vulnerable-walkers the Torah-and-prophets named the protection-substance for. FRAMEWORK-MAJOR.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 7, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 10, 8,
   '*And the whole earth has been corrupted through the works that were taught by Azâzêl: to him ascribe all sin.* 1 Enoch 10:8 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the inevitability-of-offences-in-the-present-age substance — the whole earth has-been-corrupted by the watcher-taught substance, and the offences-coming-of-necessity (Matt 18:7''s *it must needs be that offences come*) is the architectural-consequence of the corruption-already-running. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:7''s *woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come; but woe to that man by whom the offence cometh.* The inevitability does-not-excuse the man-by-whom-the-offence-comes; the architecture-of-the-fallen-age makes the offences-inevitable, and the kingdom-citizen-who-becomes-the-substance-that-causes-the-stumble has joined-himself to the watcher-substance the kingdom-came-to-undo. The framework reads this in continuity with Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 24:5-6''s *the earth also is defiled under the inhabitants thereof; because they have transgressed the laws, changed the ordinance, broken the everlasting covenant. Therefore hath the curse devoured the earth.* The earth''s-defiling and the curse''s-devouring are the architecture 1 Enoch names the source-of and the King-names the consequence-of at the millstone-warning.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 7, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 19, 1,
   '*Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods.* 1 Enoch 19:1 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the leading-astray (*planao* — the same root the King will use for the *go astray* of the sheep at vv.12-13) substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:7''s woe-against-the-man-by-whom-the-offence-comes. The fallen-watchers and their spirits operating-in-many-forms across the present-age are the architectural-substance behind every system-of-stumbling-block the King''s-millstone-warning lands-on — the institutional-Christianity''s antinomian-doctrine, the Hebrew-Roots false-inclusion gospel, the Pharisaic-traditions-of-the-elders, the Galatian-circumcision-party, the Islamic-transfer (the four-costumes per voice skill framework). The lying-spirits-leading-astray are the architecture under the doctrinal-corruptions; the kingdom-citizen-who-joins-the-corruption joins-the-substance the watchers-loosed. The framework reads this with the patience-not-condescension posture per voice skill — the little-ones-led-astray are victims-not-enemies; the systems-and-the-leadership-who-perpetuate-them are where the woe lands.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 6, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 22, 11,
   '*And these places have been made for them until the day of their judgement and until their consummation, till the consummation of their judgement is consummated for ever and ever upon the sinners.* 1 Enoch 22:11 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the place-of-the-eternal-judgment-substance — the architecture-of-judgment the King names is *better* than the substance the millstone-and-the-sea would produce. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:6''s *it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck.* The wisdom-stream had named the day-of-the-judgment-and-the-consummation as the substance-the-sinners-against-the-righteous-walk-toward; the King names the millstone-and-the-sea as the lesser-mercy compared with that judgment-substance. The framework reads the *consummation of their judgement* in continuity with the gehenna-substance of the Tanakh-*gei-Hinnom* (Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 7:32-33''s *valley of slaughter*; Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 66:24''s *worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched*) — the destruction the King names against the systems-causing-the-stumble, NOT the inherited-Christian-eternal-conscious-torment doctrine read-back into the substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 9, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 27, 2,
   '*This accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever: here shall all the accursed be gathered together who utter with their lips against Yahuah (the Lord) unseemly words and of His glory speak hard things. Here shall they be gathered together, and here shall be their place of judgement.* 1 Enoch 27:2 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the accursed-valley-of-judgment substance — the Watcher-Book passage (1 Enoch 26-27) describing the valley at the centre of the holy mountain (an explicit topographical-pointer to the *gei-Hinnom* (Valley of the sons of Hinnom) on the southern-edge of Yerushalayim (Jerusalem)). The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:9''s *gehenna of fire.* The King''s gehenna-substance is the Tanakh-and-wisdom-stream''s accursed-valley-of-judgment carried-forward; 1 Enoch 27:2 names the wisdom-stream''s identification of the place — *those who are accursed for ever* gathered for the judgment-substance at the place-of-judgment. The framework reads the substance as destruction-substance, not eternal-conscious-maintenance — *here shall be their place of judgement* is the place-where-the-judgment-is-executed, in continuity with 1 Enoch 22:11''s consummation-of-the-judgment substance and Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 66:24''s carcases-and-worm substance. The disciple cuts-off the hand-foot-eye that causes the stumble because the judgment is real.'),

  -- Thread 2: the-lord-of-the-sheep-and-the-gathering-in-the-animal-apocalypse
  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 11, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 89, 42,
   '*And the Lord of the sheep took the staff of His wrath, and cast it upon the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth, and it covered them.* 1 Enoch 89:42 names the wisdom-stream''s Animal-Apocalypse articulation of the Lord-of-the-sheep''s-substance — the One who-acts-to-deliver his sheep from the beasts-and-birds-that-devour. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:11''s *the Son of Adam is come to save that which was lost.* The Lord-of-the-sheep substance of 1 Enoch 89-90 is the wisdom-stream''s carrying-forward of the Tanakh-Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34 shepherd-substance into apocalyptic-vision-form; the King is the same Lord-of-the-sheep at the historical-pivot, walking-in-flesh to gather-the-scattered-sheep per Red Line #7''s reading of the lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) mission-scope at Matt 10:6 and Matt 15:24. FRAMEWORK-MAJOR.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 12, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 89, 54,
   '*And Enoch blessed the Lord of the sheep and said: "Blessed be Thou, O Yahuah (God), Yahuah (the Lord) of the sheep."* 1 Enoch 89:54 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the Lord-of-the-sheep-title substance — the wisdom-stream identifies the Lord-of-the-sheep with Yahuah by name. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:12''s shepherd-parable. The King''s *if a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?* is the same Lord-of-the-sheep-substance the wisdom-stream had named the substance of — the One who-acts-personally to seek-the-one-strayed. The Tanakh-and-wisdom-stream had named the substance; the King-in-flesh enacts the substance; the substance is the same shepherd at every register.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 14, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 90, 6,
   '*But behold lambs were borne by those white sheep, and they began to open their eyes and to see, and to cry to the sheep.* 1 Enoch 90:6 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the lambs-that-open-their-eyes substance — the post-judgment opening of the eyes-of-the-sheep-who-had-been-blinded under the seventy-shepherds-administration. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:14''s *it is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish.* The Father''s-will is for the lambs-that-open-their-eyes — the substance the King''s mustard-seed-faith and the disciples'' kingdom-witness gathers; the cause-and-effect-of-hearing per Red Line #11 operates in the architecture of the lambs-who-open-the-eyes being-the-substance who-hear-when-the-Shepherd-calls. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture; the kingdom-witness operationalizes it; the gathering is the Father''s-will-substance, not the universalist-overriding-determinism.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 13, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 90, 18,
   '*And I saw till all the beasts and the birds and the wild animals were gathered, and they all feared the Lord of the sheep, and they began to fall down upon his face and to worship him.* 1 Enoch 90:18 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the consummation-rejoicing the Lord-of-the-sheep walks-toward. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:13''s *if so be that he find it, verily I say unto you, he rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray.* The Lord-of-the-sheep''s-rejoicing-over-the-found-one is the substance the wisdom-stream had named at the eschatological-consummation register — the gathering-of-the-sheep at the consummation is the same shepherd-substance the King names at the assembly-internal-level. The two-levels of the shepherd-substance — the assembly''s-internal-little-ones AND the canon-wide lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) mission-scope — both derive from the same Lord-of-the-sheep architecture 1 Enoch had carried-forward from Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 10, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 40, 9,
   '*And he said unto me: "This first is Michael, the merciful and long-suffering: and the second, who is set over all sickness and all wounds, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is Phanuel."* 1 Enoch 40:9 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the four-presences-before-the-Father substance — the messengers who-have-direct-access-to-the-throne, whose-substance is mercy and long-suffering and healing and repentance-unto-hope. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:10''s *I say unto you, That in heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven.* The little-ones'' guardian-messengers operating in the Tanakh-and-Second-Temple guardian-messenger pattern (Shemot (Exodus) 23:20, Tehillim (Psalm) 91:11, Daniel 10:13, Acts 12:15, Hebrews 1:14) are the same architectural-substance 1 Enoch names for the chief-presences; the disciples'' disposition-toward-the-little-ones is bounded by the architectural-substance of the messengers'' direct-throne-access on behalf of those little-ones.'),

  -- Thread 3: the-reproof-and-restoration-procedure-in-sirach
  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 15, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 19, 13,
   '*Admonish a friend, it may be he has not done it: and if he have done it, that he may do it no more.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 19:13 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the King''s first-step assembly-discipline pattern at Matt 18:15. The framework reads the verse against *go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone: if he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother.* The wisdom-stream had named the direct-and-private admonition-of-the-friend substance at the wisdom-instruction-register; the King institutionalizes the same substance at the assembly''s-procedural-register. The wisdom-stream-procedure and the King''s-procedure cohere — confront-privately FIRST, with the substance aimed at restoration (*it may be he has not done it*; *he may do it no more*), not at public-shame or gossip. The substance reads in continuity with Vayikra (Leviticus) 19:17''s *thou shalt in any wise rebuke thy neighbour.*'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 15, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 19, 17,
   '*Admonish your neighbour before you threaten him; and not being angry, give place to the law of the Most High.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 19:17 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the disposition-the-rebuker-walks-in at the assembly-discipline procedure. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:15. The wisdom-stream names BOTH (a) the order — admonish BEFORE threatening, the substance of restoration before the substance of consequence — AND (b) the disposition — *not being angry, give place to the law of the Most High,* the wisdom-stream''s articulation that the Torah-substance, not the rebuker''s-own-anger, is the substance the rebuke-is-operating-from. The framework reads this in continuity with Galatians 6:1''s *brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye which are spiritual, restore such an one in the spirit of meekness* — the apostolic-restatement of the same disposition Sirach names the architecture for.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 16, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 19, 15,
   '*Admonish a friend: for many times it is a slander, and believe not every tale.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 19:15 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the two-or-three-witnesses substance the King institutionalizes at Matt 18:16. The framework reads the verse against *then take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established.* The wisdom-stream names the substance the witness-verification-procedure protects against — slander, the false-tale, the unverified-charge. The King applies the Tanakh-Devarim (Deuteronomy) 19:15 evidentiary-standard the wisdom-stream had named the necessity-of at the wisdom-instruction-register. The substance protects both the brother-accused (from false-charge) and the brother-accusing (from inflated-or-fabricated charge); the witnesses serve as the substance-restraint on the offended-party as much as on the accused.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 17, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 20, 2,
   '*It is much better to reprove, than to be angry secretly: and he that confesseth his fault shall be preserved from hurt.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 20:2 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the substance-of-the-open-reproof — the assembly-level-confrontation the King names at Matt 18:17''s step-three (*tell it unto the assembly*) operates in the architecture-of-open-reproof the wisdom-stream had named the substance for. The framework reads the verse against the King''s assembly-level-step. The wisdom-stream names the alternative-architecture: angry-secretly is the substance that does-not-restore; the open-reproof followed-by-the-brother''s-confession is the substance that restores. The King''s step-three is the assembly-level operationalization of the wisdom-stream''s instruction; the assembly-as-a-whole carries the open-reproof-substance at the corporate-register the wisdom-stream had carried at the wisdom-instruction-register.'),

  -- Thread 4: forgive-and-be-forgiven-the-mercy-met-with-mercy-architecture
  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 21, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 27, 30,
   '*Malice and wrath, even these are abominations; and the sinful man shall have them both.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 27:30 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the disposition-the-King-is-forming-against at Kefa (Peter)''s v.21 question. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:21. The wisdom-stream had named malice and wrath as abominations-before-Yahuah at the wisdom-instruction-register; Kefa''s *how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? till seven times?* is the disciple-substance still-counting-the-offences, and the King''s answer presses-past-the-counting into the disposition-of-no-malice. The framework reads this in continuity with the kingdom-citizens'' fruits-of-the-Spirit substance (Galatians 5:22-23''s love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness) the new-heart of Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27 forms-the-walker-into. FRAMEWORK-MAJOR.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 22, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 28, 2,
   '*Forgive your neighbour the hurt that he has done to you, so shall your sins also be forgiven when you prayest.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 28:2 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the conditional-forgiveness-architecture the King names at Matt 18:21-22 and parable-extends at vv.23-35. The framework reads the verse against the King''s *seventy times seven* answer + the unforgiving-servant parable + the chapter-closing *so likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not* (v.35). The wisdom-stream had named the substance directly: forgive-the-neighbour, and your-sins-shall-also-be-forgiven; the conditional-substance the King''s parable extends into full narrative-form was already-articulated at the wisdom-stream-register. The framework reads this in continuity with Matt 6:14-15''s Lord''s-Prayer conditional-substance — *for if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you: But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.* The architecture-of-mercy-met-with-mercy runs the King''s-teaching from the Sermon through the assembly-discourse; the wisdom-stream had named the substance the King operationalizes.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 33, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 28, 3,
   '*One man bears hatred against another, and does he seek pardon from Yahuah (God)?* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 28:3 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the unforgiving-servant''s-grotesque-architecture the King names at Matt 18:33. The framework reads the verse against the lord''s charge to the first-servant: *O thou wicked servant, I forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me: shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on thee?* The wisdom-stream had named the grotesque-substance: one-man-bears-hatred-against-another and yet seeks-pardon-from-Yahuah for himself; the parable shows the same architecture in narrative-form — the first-servant has-been-forgiven and refuses-to-forgive. The lord''s-wrath-and-revocation-of-the-forgiveness in the parable is the same architectural-substance Sirach had named the wisdom-instruction-substance-against. The kingdom-citizen''s-substance must match the substance-received; the architecture is mercy-met-with-mercy at every register the wisdom-stream-and-the-King-and-the-apostles articulate.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 35, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 28, 7,
   '*Remember the commandments, and bear no malice to your neighbour: remember the covenant of the Highest, and wink at ignorance.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 28:7 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the heart-Torah-substance the King''s chapter-closing v.35 lands-on. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:35''s *so likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.* The wisdom-stream had named the substance directly: remember-the-commandments AND bear-no-malice to your-neighbour; remember-the-covenant-of-the-Most-High AND wink-at-ignorance. The two-substances are NOT in tension; the two-substances are one-substance — the Torah-internalized produces the substance-of-no-malice; the substance-of-no-malice is the operation-of-the-Torah-internalized. The framework reads this in continuity with Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:33''s new-covenant law-in-the-inward-parts and Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27''s new-heart-and-Spirit-causing-the-walking — the wisdom-stream had named the substance the new-covenant brings-to-completion. The grace-that-can-be-lost architecture per Red Line #10 operates here: the walker who-walks-the-substance walks-through-the-door-home; the walker-who-bears-malice-against-the-brother has-not-walked-the-substance-the-grace-was-given-to-form.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 35, 'pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 62, 3,
   '*Love ye one another from the heart; and if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him.* Testament of Gad 62:3 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the heart-substance + the speak-peaceably-to-the-sinning-brother substance the King''s chapter-arc lands-on at v.35 and operationalizes at vv.15-17. The framework reads the verse against the unforgiving-servant parable + the assembly-discipline procedure. The Testament-of-Gad''s confessional-instruction — Gad confessing his-own-hatred-of-Joseph and the substance-of-repentance he-came-to — names the heart-substance the King''s *from your hearts* (v.35) requires. The framework reads this as the wisdom-stream''s direct prefiguring of both ends of the chapter-arc: (a) the v.15 first-step *go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone* operates from the substance Testament of Gad names — *speak peaceably to him*; (b) the v.35 chapter-closing *if ye from your hearts forgive not* operates from the substance Testament of Gad names — *love ye one another from the heart.* The wisdom-stream had carried the heart-substance; the King''s assembly-architecture institutionalizes the heart-substance at the kingdom-citizens'' corporate-register.'),

  -- Thread 5: the-greatness-as-humility-and-the-proud-cast-down-in-the-wisdom-stream
  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 3, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 3, 18,
   '*The greater you are, the more humble thyself, and you shall find favour before Yahuah (God).* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 3:18 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the kingdom-inversion-of-greatness substance the King teaches at Matt 18:3-4. The framework reads the verse against *except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall not enter into the kingdom of heaven. Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.* The wisdom-stream had named the substance directly: the-greater-you-are, the-more-humble-yourself; the substance the King teaches at the assembly-disposition register the wisdom-stream had taught at the wisdom-instruction register. The framework reads this in continuity with the Tanakh-*anawim* (humble-poor) substance pattern (Tehillim (Psalm) 131:1-2; Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 57:15; Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 66:2; Mishlei (Proverbs) 22:4); the apostolic-restatement at 1 Peter 5:5 (citing Mishlei (Proverbs) 3:34) and Yaaqov (James) 4:10. The kingdom-citizen''s greatness is measured by the depth of the humility-substance, not by the height of the position-substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 4, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 10, 14,
   '*Yahuah (God) has cast down the thrones of proud princes, and set up the meek in their stead.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 10:14 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the kingdom-inversion-of-thrones substance — the proud-cast-down and the meek-set-up at the same divine-action. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:4''s *whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.* The wisdom-stream names the same inversion the King names — the substance the assembly is to walk-in is the substance the Father acts-by at the eschatological-day. The framework reads this in continuity with Mary''s Magnificat at Luke 1:51-52 (*he hath put down the mighty from their seats, and exalted them of low degree*) and the post-resurrection apostolic-restatement at 1 Corinthians 1:26-29 (*Elohim (God) hath chosen the foolish things of the world to confound the wise; and Elohim (God) hath chosen the weak things of the world to confound the things which are mighty*).'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 18, 1, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 10, 7,
   '*Pride is hateful before Yahuah (God) and man: and by both does one commit iniquity.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 10:7 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the disposition-the-King-is-confronting at the disciples'' v.1 hierarchy-question. The framework reads the verse against Matt 18:1''s *who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?* The disciples have-imbibed-substantially of the kingdom-substance over months of ministry; the disciples have-not-yet-shed the natural-kingdoms'' hierarchy-substance the wisdom-stream had named the pride-substance for. The framework reads the verse in continuity with the Markan-parallel''s preserved-detail at Mark 9:33-34 (the disciples-had-been-disputing-on-the-road *who should be the greatest*) — the pride-substance the wisdom-stream names is the substance operating-in the disciples'' road-side-dispute. The King''s-acted-parable of the child-in-the-midst is the substance-correction the wisdom-stream had instructed-toward.')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s155_xref_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug   = i.src_edition
                           AND sv.book_slug      = i.src_slug
                           AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                           AND sv.verse_number   = i.src_v
  JOIN _s155_xref_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug   = i.tgt_edition
                           AND tv.book_slug      = i.tgt_slug
                           AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                           AND tv.verse_number   = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

